  "notes": [
    "Percentages total to 100 per settlement group.",
    "Base regional pools use the first 3 distinct troop level tiers.",
    "Settlement-specific (household) pools use the first 2 distinct troop level tiers.",
    "In a TOWN where both apply, the regular line totals 60 percent and the household / settlement-specific line 40 percent (20 until 2026-09-13; raised on player feedback that the household lines were too rare next to the regional levies).",
    "A CASTLE that has a household line offers only that line: Glanhir (Ringlo Vale), Morlad (Blackroot Vale), Bar-en-Siril (Serelond), Cair Andros, Caras Tolfalas, Linhir.",
    "A village named for a vale follows the vale, not its region: Upper Ringló and Vale Village (Ringlo Vale), Morlad's four villages and Blackroot Village Haven (Blackroot Vale). Every other village keeps its regional line, except Bar Melui's three, which have shared the town's Lossarnach Regular + Noble group since before 2026-07-27 and were left as found.",
    "The Anorien capitals Minas Tirith and Osgiliath run 50 regular / 40 specific / 10 Ithilien Ranger; Cair Andros runs 90 Cair Andros / 10 Ithilien Ranger.",
    "Where only one pool applies, that pool totals 100 percent.",
    "Trailing remainders absorb into the last troop of a split (13.3333 / 13.3333 / 13.3334) so each group totals exactly 100.",
    "If a rule says only a settlement, only that town/castle receives the specific pool, not its bound villages.",
    "Ithil Guard applies to town_ES2 only when Minas Morgul / Minas Ithil is owned by Gondor."
